 in Q4 2025 and +1.8% in Q1 2026, so growth has been slowing (CEA Q2 2026 report, n3.d3, n3.d5).\n- The CEA says shipments trail orders by about two quarters. A Q2 2026 slowdown therefore reflects orders placed around late 2025, and it points to soft shipments into at least H2 2026.\n- Voltaris quarterly revenue (n3.d4) was C$905M, C$960M, C$980M and C$890M for 2025Q3 to 2026Q2. Q2 2026 fell about 9% from Q1. The last four quarters sum to about C$3.73B.\n\n**What the guidance requires**\n- C$4.2B is about 12.6% above the trailing-four-quarter total of C$3.73B. It is also about 17% above an annualised Q2 2026 run rate of C$3.56B.\n- That means roughly C$1.05B per quarter through 2027, higher than any quarter in the series.\n- Industry shipments are shrinking, so the growth would have to come from share gains or pricing.\n\n**Caveats**\n- n2 found that H1 2026 orders were up 11% year on year, led by utility and data-centre customers (n2.d5). If Voltaris is taking share, orders would reach revenue with a lag and could support a 2027 recovery. I didn't verify that, and I haven't seen Voltaris's share.\n- With the share data missing, this is an inference from the industry trend and Voltaris's revenue run rate.\n- I estimate 2027 revenue at roughly C$3.7–4.0B on industry data alone. Reaching C$4.2B would need Voltaris to outgrow a declining industry by about 10 points or more.\n- Whether orders and backlog close that gap is n2's question.","ttft_ms":1925,"type":"result","duration_ms":29949,"uuid":"6cf97962-758b-455d-9e0d-8c671046da77","ttft_stream_ms":1030,"time_to_request_ms":76,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":10,"message_prep":3,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_sche